asset:        1110-extra.aep
title:        After Effects project: extra HDR Highlight Compression (Amount 25, 50, 75) and Echo (Blend operator with several echoes, Composite In Back, Composite In Front) variants
author:       vangel76 (contributor)
source:       original work; group 1110-extra of tools/aep/importer-samples/jsx/g7-extra.jsx (EffectCraft issues 3123 and 3124); generation notes docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md
license:      MIT OR Apache-2.0
license-file: ../LICENSE-MIT, ../LICENSE-APACHE
added:        2026-11-05 by @vangel76
notes:        Generated from scratch by the contributor with Adobe After Effects 2026 (26.2.1x2) on Windows 11 as their own test data for the effectcraft-aep tests; it holds only synthetic project structure, no third-party footage, template or personal data, and no Adobe sample project, preset or asset was used. The generic variants of both effects plus the extra ones (26 variants, aep/readbacks/1110-extra.json). Sources: the SRC test card and aep/media/crypto-320x180.exr. 32 bpc, working space None. Saved-file cleanup, in this order: (1) the footage link of the EXR names a contributor-made file that is not included here (aep/media/ holds the same EXR); its stored path and the host name were replaced by neutral ones of the same length (tools/aep/scrub.py); the XMP packet after the project container was replaced by the packet of empty.aep; (2) tools/aep/scrub-uninit.py zeroed what After Effects had written from uninitialised memory (the unread part of the EXR footage options record (9616 bytes, after byte 47) was zeroed; it held text from other process memory; details in docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md); (3) the embedded ICC profile of the working space was replaced by a description-only stub (tools/aep/stubicc.rs: 128-byte header, one `desc` tag, no colour data), which keeps the profile name for metadata tests and is not a colour-transform oracle. Final bytes checked with tools/aep/inspect-embedded.py (raw, base64 and hex, with the local user, host and folder names as --forbid): CLEAN. A chunk-by-chunk comparison with the saved file and an import of both files with the importer show that only those records changed (docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md).
